// A PNG reader — the container, the deflate stream inside it, the filters under that, and the
// pixels under those.
//
// The axis this owns is **the byte level**: a format somebody else defined, where being wrong by
// one byte is silent. Nothing here is a design of ours to get right. The signature is eight
// specific bytes, the chunk lengths are big-endian, the bit stream inside them is little-endian,
// the Huffman codes inside *that* are packed the other way up again, the filters are modulo 256,
// and the two checksums are computed by two unrelated methods. A reader that gets any of it wrong
// still produces an image; it just produces the wrong one. That is why every check here compares a
// value somebody else computed — the fixtures came out of a different encoder, and the checksum
// vectors are the published ones.
//
// What writing it turned up:
//
//   * **Embedded binary data wanted a multi-line literal, and it wanted one that removes lines
//     rather than keeping them.** This program was the reason the text block was specified, and the
//     reason it was specified the way it is: what a file written as hex needs is not line breaks in
//     its value but one constant written over as many lines as it takes to read. So the ten files
//     here are now text blocks whose lines join at the trailing backslash, and each is a single
//     constant where the `+=` chain allocated and copied once per line. An array literal would
//     still be one line of two hundred numbers.
//   * **A table the format writes down, and a table you have to derive, are two different asks.**
//     This program wanted both and reported them as one. The first has since been answered: `val`
//     is static read-only storage with an address, so `inflate`'s five deflate tables — the
//     code-length order, and the base and extra-bit counts for lengths and distances — are module
//     members laid into the object file, where they used to be array literals rebuilt on every
//     call. The second is still open: a CRC is a table lookup in every implementation ever written,
//     and this one is computed a bit at a time — eight times the work — because the 256 entries are
//     *derived* rather than written down, and a `val`'s initializer must be a value as it stands.
//     Static storage with a **computed** initializer is a further feature, and it needs a rule for
//     what order such initializers run in (`13 §7`).
//     The array bounds were the other half, and they were answered by `const`. Every one of them
//     names a number the format chose — `[max_lit + max_dist]u8` where this first said `[320]u8`
//     and meant "286 + 30, rounded up".
//   * **A decoder's intermediate storage was in its signature.** `decode` took three buffers, and
//     two of them were its own internals: somewhere to gather the compressed data, somewhere to
//     unpack it to. The caller had to supply both, in sizes it could not work out without reading
//     the header — which happens inside — so the finding was not that a function was awkward but
//     that the gap was visible in the API, and there was a `NoRoom` fault whose only cause was the
//     signature. Answered: an array form written where a `[]T` is expected makes storage of its own
//     and the view owns it, so a length may be computed rather than declared. `decode` now takes a
//     file and returns an image, `NoRoom` is gone, and the two checks that existed to provoke it
//     are gone with it.
//   * **`Result[unit, E]` was missing here too**, in a program with nothing else in common with a
//     parser. Eight functions across the two modules returned `Result[bool, Fault]` with a `bool`
//     nobody read. The compiler front end that found this first made it look like a property of
//     parsers; a bit-stream decoder finding the same thing is what made it structural, and it is
//     now answered — `unit` is zero-sized, so it may be a payload (`00 §12`).
//   * **A struct member cannot say `private`.** `Image.index` is nobody's business but `at`'s, and
//     there is no way to write that down — the same gap the compiler's lexer hit, from the other
//     side.
//   * **Almost every loop here was first written as a `while` with its increment at the foot of the
//     body**, which is what a byte-level program is mostly made of. Most of them wanted the range
//     loop that already existed and were simply not written as one; the rest wanted a stride or two
//     counters at once, which is the three-clause `for` that was added afterwards — see `unhex`,
//     walking a hex string two characters at a time while filling a buffer one byte at a time.
//
// And the thing that went *right*, which for this program is the finding that matters most:
// **the corrected operator precedence is worth what it cost.** `c & 1u32 != 0u32`,
// `1u32 << k - 1u32`, `x + predicted & 255`, `u32(b) << 24u32 | u32(b) << 16u32` — every one of
// those reads as intended with no parentheses, and every one of them needs them in C. This is the
// first program in the set that is nothing *but* bit manipulation, so it is the first one in a
// position to say so. The trade is real and shows up once: shifts binding like multiplication
// means `first + count << 1` is `first + (count << 1)`, so the canonical-Huffman step that wants
// the other grouping is the one place here that had to say which.

// The checks. Every line of output begins `ok`, so the whole of stdout is the assertion.

private read32(b: []u8, at: usize) -> u32
    u32(b[at]) << 24u32 | u32(b[at + 1]) << 16u32 | u32(b[at + 2]) << 8u32 | u32(b[at + 3])

private write32(b: []u8, at: usize, v: u32)
    b[at] = u8(v >> 24u32)
    b[at + 1] = u8(v >> 16u32 & 255u32)
    b[at + 2] = u8(v >> 8u32 & 255u32)
    b[at + 3] = u8(v & 255u32)
end write32

// Put a chunk's checksum back after tampering with it, so that a test of what the *reader* makes
// of a changed header is not answered by the checksum first.
private reseal(b: []u8, at: usize)
    var len = usize(read32(b, at))

    write32(b, at + 8 + len, crc32(b[at + 4..<at + 8 + len]))
end reseal

private matches(out: []u8, n: usize, want: string) -> bool
    if n != want.len then return false

    for i in 0..<n
        if out[i] != want[i] then return false

    true
end matches

same(label: string, got: string, want: string)
    if got == want then print(s"ok    $label -> $got")
    else print(s"FAIL  $label -> $got (wanted $want)")
end same

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- checksums

// `s.bytes` is the seam between the two halves of this program: text on one side, the byte view a
// checksum works over on the other, no copy in between.
crc(label: string, text: string, want: string)
    same(label, f"${crc32(text.bytes)}%08x", want)

adler(label: string, text: string, want: string)
    same(label, f"${inflate.adler32(text.bytes)}%08x", want)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- inflate

unpacks(label: string, hex: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var out: [512]u8
    var n = unhex(hex, src[..])

    inflate.zlib(src[..<n], out[..]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${inflate.describe(f)}")
        Ok(k) ->
            if matches(out[..], k, want) then print(s"ok    $label -> ${str(k)} bytes")
            else print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${str(k)} bytes")
end unpacks

// A stream with one byte changed, which is how a decoder finds out whether it is checking or
// merely reading.
mangles(label: string, hex: string, at: usize, value: u8, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var out: [512]u8
    var n = unhex(hex, src[..])

    src[at] = value

    inflate.zlib(src[..<n], out[..]) match
        Ok(k) -> print(s"FAIL  $label unpacked ${str(k)} bytes")
        Err(f) -> same(label, inflate.describe(f), want)
end mangles

chopped(label: string, hex: string, keep: usize, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var out: [512]u8

    unhex(hex, src[..])

    inflate.zlib(src[..<keep], out[..]) match
        Ok(k) -> print(s"FAIL  $label unpacked ${str(k)} bytes")
        Err(f) -> same(label, inflate.describe(f), want)
end chopped

// A bare deflate stream, with no wrapper to check it, which is the only way to ask what the
// decoder does with bits no encoder would have written.
refuses(label: string, hex: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var out: [512]u8
    var n = unhex(hex, src[..])

    inflate.raw(src[..<n], out[..]) match
        Ok(k) -> print(s"FAIL  $label unpacked ${str(k)} bytes")
        Err(f) -> same(label, inflate.describe(f), want)
end refuses

crowded(label: string, hex: string, room: usize, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var out: [512]u8
    var n = unhex(hex, src[..])

    inflate.zlib(src[..<n], out[..<room]) match
        Ok(k) -> print(s"FAIL  $label unpacked ${str(k)} bytes")
        Err(f) -> same(label, inflate.describe(f), want)
end crowded

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- images

header(label: string, file: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${describe(f)}")
        Ok(img) -> same(label, f"${img.width}%dx${img.height}%d type ${img.kind}%d", want)
end header

pixel(label: string, file: string, x: usize, y: usize, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${describe(f)}")
        Ok(img) ->
            var p = img.at(x, y)

            same(label, f"${p.r}%d ${p.g}%d ${p.b}%d ${p.a}%d", want)
end pixel

// Every sample of the five-row image, against the arithmetic that generated it. One check rather
// than sixty, because sixty checks of the same shape say nothing sixty times.
sweep(label: string, file: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${describe(f)}")
        Ok(img) ->
            var wrong = 0

            for y in 0..<img.height
                for x in 0..<img.width
                    var p = img.at(x, y)
                    var base = int(y * 4 + x) * 3

                    if int(p.r) != base || int(p.g) != base + 7 || int(p.b) != base + 14 then wrong += 1

            same(label, s"${str(wrong)} wrong", "0 wrong")
end sweep

// An image small enough to print, which is the most direct check there is: if a filter were undone
// wrongly, or a row were read at the wrong offset, the picture would say so.
art(label: string, file: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${describe(f)}")
        Ok(img) ->
            var out = ""

            for y in 0..<img.height
                for x in 0..<img.width
                    out += if img.at(x, y).r > 127u8 then "#" else "."

                out += "\n"

            if out == want then print(s"ok    $label")
            else print(s"FAIL  $label\n$out")
end art

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- broken images

broken(label: string, file: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end broken

cut(label: string, file: string, keep: usize, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8

    unhex(file, src[..])

    decode(src[..<keep]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end cut

// One byte changed and nothing else, so the checksum notices.
scratched(label: string, file: string, at: usize, value: u8, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    src[at] = value

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end scratched

// One byte changed and the checksum put back, so the reader has to be the one that objects.
edited(label: string, file: string, at: usize, value: u8, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    src[at] = value
    reseal(src[..], 8usize)

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end edited

// A byte of the compressed pixel data changed, its chunk resealed. Nothing in the container layer
// can object, so whatever objects does so from inside the deflate stream.
spoiled(label: string, file: string, chunk: usize, at: usize, value: u8, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    src[at] = value
    reseal(src[..], chunk)

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end spoiled

// A chunk given a different name, its checksum recomputed to match. The case of the first letter
// is the only difference between a chunk a reader may skip and one it may not.
renamed(label: string, file: string, at: usize, name: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    for i in 0usize..<4usize
        src[at + 4 + i] = name[i]

    reseal(src[..], at)

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Ok(img) -> print(s"FAIL  $label decoded")
        Err(f) -> same(label, describe(f), want)
end renamed

// The same tampering, where the new name is one a reader is allowed to walk past.
tolerated(label: string, file: string, at: usize, name: string, want: string)
    var src: [256]u8
    var n = unhex(file, src[..])

    for i in 0usize..<4usize
        src[at + 4 + i] = name[i]

    reseal(src[..], at)

    decode(src[..<n]) match
        Err(f) -> print(s"FAIL  $label -> ${describe(f)}")
        Ok(img) -> same(label, f"${img.width}%dx${img.height}%d type ${img.kind}%d", want)
end tolerated

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ what to expect

squares() -> string
    var s = ""

    for i in 0..<60
        if i > 0 then s += " "

        s += str(i * i)

    s
end squares

repeated(c: string, n: int) -> string
    var s = ""

    for i in 0..<n
        s += c

    s
end repeated

checkerboard() -> string
    var s = ""

    for y in 0..<8
        s += if y % 2 == 0 then "#.#.#.#.\n" else ".#.#.#.#\n"

    s
end checkerboard

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the runs

print("-- checksums")
crc("the checksum of nothing at all", "", "00000000")
crc("of one letter", "a", "e8b7be43")
crc("of three", "abc", "352441c2")
crc("of a sentence", "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog", "414fa339")
adler("the other checksum of nothing", "", "00000001")
adler("of three letters", "abc", "024d0127")
adler("of the same sentence", "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog", "5bdc0fda")

print("-- deflate")
unpacks("a stored block", zstored(), "hello, world")
unpacks("a fixed-code block", zfixed(), "abracadabra abracadabra")
unpacks("a dynamic-code block", zdyn(), squares())
unpacks("a match that reads what it is writing", zrun(), repeated("z", 300))

print("-- streams the decoder refuses")
mangles("a compression method that is not deflate", zstored(), 0usize, 0x79u8, "compression method 9 is not deflate")
mangles("header bits that do not check out", zstored(), 1usize, 0x00u8, "the header's check bits do not agree")
mangles("a window wider than any encoder uses", zstored(), 0usize, 0x88u8, "a window wider than the format allows")
mangles("a stream that wants a dictionary", zstored(), 1usize, 0x20u8, "a stream wanting a dictionary it was not given")
mangles("a byte of the payload changed", zstored(), 7usize, 0x69u8, "the checksum says 1d540489 and the bytes say 1d60048a")
chopped("a stream that stops in the middle", zfixed(), 8usize, "the stream ends in the middle of something")
crowded("more output than there is room for", zrun(), 100usize, "no room left for what the stream unpacks to")
refuses("a block of a kind the format reserves", "07", "a block of no known kind")
refuses("a stored length that disagrees with its complement", "0105000000", "a stored block whose length and complement disagree")
refuses("a stored block longer than what is left", "010500faff", "the stream ends in the middle of something")
refuses("a match reaching before the start", faraway(), "a match reaching 5 bytes back, before anything was written")
refuses("a code the fixed table leaves undefined", nosuchcode(), "a code that stands for nothing")
refuses("a length symbol past the end of the table", toolong(), "length symbol 286 is past the end of the table")
refuses("a table claiming more codes than there are", toomany(), "a code table claiming more codes than its lengths leave room for")

print("-- headers")
header("a truecolour image", rgb(), "2x2 type 2")
header("a greyscale one", gray(), "4x4 type 0")
header("a paletted one", paletted(), "4x4 type 3")
header("one with an alpha channel", rgba(), "2x2 type 6")
header("greyscale with alpha", grayalpha(), "2x2 type 4")
header("and one big enough to look at", checker(), "8x8 type 0")

print("-- pixels")
pixel("red, at the top left", rgb(), 0usize, 0usize, "255 0 0 255")
pixel("green beside it", rgb(), 1usize, 0usize, "0 255 0 255")
pixel("blue below", rgb(), 0usize, 1usize, "0 0 255 255")
pixel("yellow in the corner", rgb(), 1usize, 1usize, "255 255 0 255")
pixel("the darkest grey", gray(), 0usize, 0usize, "0 0 0 255")
pixel("the end of the first row", gray(), 3usize, 0usize, "51 51 51 255")
pixel("the start of the second", gray(), 0usize, 1usize, "68 68 68 255")
pixel("the lightest grey", gray(), 3usize, 3usize, "255 255 255 255")
pixel("a palette entry", paletted(), 1usize, 0usize, "255 0 0 255")
pixel("the entry after it", paletted(), 2usize, 0usize, "0 255 0 255")
pixel("the last entry", paletted(), 3usize, 0usize, "0 0 255 255")
pixel("an index that wrapped around", paletted(), 3usize, 3usize, "0 255 0 255")
pixel("a transparent pixel", rgba(), 0usize, 0usize, "255 0 0 0")
pixel("a third of the way opaque", rgba(), 1usize, 0usize, "0 255 0 85")
pixel("two thirds", rgba(), 0usize, 1usize, "0 0 255 170")
pixel("and solid", rgba(), 1usize, 1usize, "255 255 255 255")
pixel("grey with an alpha of its own", grayalpha(), 1usize, 0usize, "85 85 85 170")
pixel("and the one that vanishes", grayalpha(), 1usize, 1usize, "255 255 255 0")
pixel("a row stored rather than compressed", stored(), 0usize, 0usize, "0 0 0 255")
pixel("further along the same row", stored(), 5usize, 0usize, "80 80 80 255")

print("-- filters")
pixel("a row filtered by nothing at all", filtered(), 0usize, 0usize, "0 7 14 255")
pixel("a row filtered against the pixel to its left", filtered(), 3usize, 1usize, "21 28 35 255")
pixel("a row filtered against the row above", filtered(), 0usize, 2usize, "24 31 38 255")
pixel("a row filtered against the average of both", filtered(), 2usize, 3usize, "42 49 56 255")
pixel("a row filtered by the Paeth predictor", filtered(), 3usize, 4usize, "57 64 71 255")
sweep("every sample of all five rows", filtered())
art("a picture, as the surest check of all", checker(), checkerboard())

print("-- chunks")
header("ancillary chunks are skipped", extra(), "2x2 type 2")
pixel("and the image around them survives", extra(), 1usize, 1usize, "255 255 0 255")
header("image data split across three chunks", split(), "2x2 type 2")
pixel("reads as one stream", split(), 0usize, 1usize, "0 0 255 255")
renamed("a critical chunk nobody knows", extra(), 33usize, "ZZZZ", "a chunk named 'ZZZZ' that must be understood and is not")
tolerated("the same chunk, its name made lowercase", extra(), 33usize, "zZZZ", "2x2 type 2")

print("-- files the reader refuses")
scratched("something that is not a PNG", rgb(), 1usize, 0x00u8, "not a PNG at all")
scratched("a chunk that does not match its checksum", rgb(), 19usize, 0x03u8, "the chunk at 8 does not match its checksum")
cut("a file that stops inside a chunk", rgb(), 40usize, "the file ends inside the chunk at 33")
cut("a file with nothing to end it", rgb(), 65usize, "the last chunk is not the end chunk")
edited("sixteen bits a sample", rgb(), 24usize, 16u8, "16 bits a sample, and this reader knows only 8")
edited("a colour type that does not exist", rgb(), 25usize, 5u8, "colour type 5 is not one of the five")
edited("compressed by something else", rgb(), 26usize, 1u8, "compressed by something other than deflate")
edited("filtered by something else", rgb(), 27usize, 1u8, "filtered by a method this format does not have")
edited("an interlaced image", rgb(), 28usize, 1u8, "interlaced, and this reader reads rows in order")
edited("an image no pixels wide", rgb(), 19usize, 0u8, "an image with no pixels in it")
edited("a height the pixels do not fill", rgb(), 23usize, 3u8, "the rows need 21 bytes and the data unpacks to 14")
renamed("a header that is not the first chunk", rgb(), 8usize, "iHDR", "the header is not the first chunk")
renamed("a second header, further in", extra(), 33usize, "IHDR", "the header is not the first chunk")
renamed("an image whose pixels were skipped", rgb(), 33usize, "zdat", "no image data")
renamed("a paletted image with no palette", paletted(), 33usize, "pLTE", "a paletted image with no palette")
broken("a row filtered by a rule that does not exist", badfilter(), "row 0 claims filter 5")
spoiled("a byte of the pixel data changed", rgb(), 33usize, 45usize, 0x00u8, "the checksum says 1eef04fc and the bytes say 00f200f1")
spoiled("the byte before it, where the codes are", rgb(), 33usize, 44usize, 0x00u8, "a match reaching 6530 bytes back, before anything was written")
